{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1271591-lesser-known-gods-domains-5e","id":1271591,"title":"Lesser Known Gods Domains (5e)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scarred Lands"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-28T14:55:38-08:00","id":1271591,"title":"Lesser Known Gods Domains (5e)","content":"So Strange Lands has a number of deities. Especially in Asherak.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on what domains those gods would have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13194-psyclus","name":"Psyclus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T16:01:56-08:00","id":1271608,"title":"","content":"Very interesting question ^^ Here are some gut-feeling possibilities, without having given it too much thoughts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ashumas -&gt; Knowledge<br /> D'Shahn -&gt; Justice<br /> Elamash -&gt; War? [maybe Trickery or Nature? difficult to say, really]<br /> The Flayed God -&gt; Death<br /> Gamgal -&gt; Justice [alternatively, Grave domain from Xanathar would be adequate]<br /> Immatuk -&gt; Knowledge [or Magic ?]<br /> Kadeshu -&gt; Freedom<br /> Otossal -&gt; Death<br /> Sarhari -&gt; Life [maybe Nature ?]<br /> Subastas -&gt; Light<br /> Tamul -&gt; Knowledge<br /> Tukulto -&gt; Nature [or maybe Freedom ?]<br /> <br /> And demi-gods from The Divine and the Defeated<br /> <br /> Ashparal -&gt; Nature<br /> Fraelhia -&gt; Storm<br /> Imal Wheatsheaf -&gt; Nature [or maybe Life ?]<br /> Katashama -&gt; Light<br /> Laathsaal -&gt; Nature [or maybe Magic ?]<br /> Luchanig -&gt; Nature [or maybe Trickery ?]<br /> Trelu -&gt; Trickery<br /> Volskalka -&gt; War<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Alain%20Giorla\" target=\"_blank\">Slarecian Vault contributions</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5793-haaz","name":"haaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T08:20:44-08:00","id":1272626,"title":"","content":"Hmm... as I think abou tit, Elamash and Subastas... I wonder if, in the new scheme of things, they make for Lesser Titans more than Demigods (rigorous theological debate on the essence of divinity and what makes a demigod as opposed to a Titan GO!).<br /> <br /> That's a pretty good list. Elamash definitely doesn't seem to fit the current 5E domains. For Immatuk, I think Knowledge does fit a bit better than Magic, as wizardry was described as &quot;by extension&quot; for her.<br /> <br /> Sarhari is a... strange one. She should almost have Life based on her role as custodian of the soul.<br /> <br /> Tulkulti: nature perhaps with a forced water theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13194-psyclus","name":"Psyclus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-04T03:40:45-08:00","id":1272810,"title":"","content":"Re-reading Elamash entry in Strange Lands, maybe Dominion could fit?<br /> <br /> As to whether they are lesser titans and demi-gods, here is my (very personal) take on how to reconciliate the views of both the old and the new edition: lesser titans are technically divine beings (aka, all children of the titans are deities), but a) they didn't manage to create a cult following them and/or b) they sided with the titans during the Divine War. So the other gods told everyone that these creatures were &quot;lesser titans&quot; (aka not gods) so that they could be identified as enemies and killed/destroyed without second thought or too much drama. If you think of all the cleanup they had to do after killing Orathel and Urkanthus, maybe they didn't want to do the same for the gazillions other children that the titans had. And it wouldn't be the first time that the gods bend the truth to hide their mistakes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Alain%20Giorla\" target=\"_blank\">Slarecian Vault contributions</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5793-haaz","name":"haaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T06:19:19-07:00","id":1411067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1271591-lesser-known-gods-domains-5e?p=1272810#post1272810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re-reading Elamash entry in Strange Lands, maybe Dominion could fit?<br /> <br /> As to whether they are lesser titans and demi-gods, here is my (very personal) take on how to reconciliate the views of both the old and the new edition: lesser titans are technically divine beings (aka, all children of the titans are deities), but a) they didn't manage to create a cult following them and/or b) they sided with the titans during the Divine War. So the other gods told everyone that these creatures were &quot;lesser titans&quot; (aka not gods) so that they could be identified as enemies and killed/destroyed without second thought or too much drama. If you think of all the cleanup they had to do after killing Orathel and Urkanthus, maybe they didn't want to do the same for the gazillions other children that the titans had. And it wouldn't be the first time that the gods bend the truth to hide their mistakes...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say the issue might be more complex than just a title, considering Orathel, even though mostly unamed, still is very much defined as a &quot;dead god&quot; and not a lesser titan like Spiragos for example.<br /> <br /> That said, i'll be the first to admit i know little to nothing on the deities of Asherak and how they relate or not to those of Ghelspad, but feel calling someone lesser titan, demigod or whatever should involve more than just enmity or neutrality during the conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}